                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "+ Original twist on the tower defense genre\n+ Great multiplayer feature where other players can transport your goods where you need them\n+ Nice player-to-player trading system, though sadly few people still play it.\n+ Good variety of enemies\n\n\n- The difficulty spikes are sometimes absurd\n- Sadly, the game cannot be paused, so don't expect any proper planning. It's just about quickly placing towers ASAP and finding at least somewhat sensible positions\n- The controls feel horribly designed. Keyboard shortcuts often don't work properly, and the modules look so similar that they easily blend together. When things get hectic, it’s hard to tell them apart in time.\n- RNG bullshit... enemies can attack from all sides, while bosses can spawn from completely random directions. If the boss spawns from the one side you didn't cover, too bad you're screwed.\n- In my opinion, there are way too few towers and several of them are completely useless\n- Extremely repetitive... with basically the exact same thing happening in every new sector\n- Mission where cargo randomly teleports around the ship is stupid idea rly\n- Waiting for server response :)\n\n\n\nIt was honestly so close to being a unique and very high-quality game, but the developers decided to completely and utterly screw up the concept.\nThis piece of crap deserves nothing more than a Mixed rating.",
